\paragraph{Additional directions.} Ten further experiments confirm the pattern (Appendix Table~\ref{tab:additional_interventions}). Formal verification via code generation (PROVE) achieves only 15.2\% compilable programs with $\Delta = -1.9$\,pp. Iterative CEGIS refinement oscillates after round~1 without convergence. Logprob-based filtering (DeepConf) finds near-zero separation between correct and incorrect traces ($\Delta_{\text{logprob}} = 0.006$). Cross-model SICA with three families reduces $\kappa$ from 0.53 to 0.42 but yields $\Delta = -0.49$\,pp ($p = 1.0$). Problem perturbation \emph{increases} $\kappa$ to 0.70 (anti-effect). MIN-UNSAT objective produces $\Delta = -6.5$\,pp. $\kappa$-aware weighted voting yields $\Delta = 0$ across 11 conditions. Z3-based trace filtering achieves 49.1\% precision with $\Delta = -0.49$\,pp. Bootstrapped gold constraints oscillate like CEGIS. ASCII format perturbation yields negligible $\kappa$ reduction (0.39 $\to$ 0.36).

